---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { SITE, DONATE, ANALYTICS, NEEDS_COOKIE_CONSENT } from "../data/site";

/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * Written to describe what this site actually does — not a generic template.
 * It reflects the real configuration: which analytics are enabled, whether a
 * donation platform is connected, and the photo-consent practice the brief
 * asks AVID to establish before the first shoot.
 *
 * NOTE FOR AVID: this is a clear, honest, plain-language policy, but it is not
 * legal advice. Have it reviewed by a Canadian lawyer before you begin
 * collecting personal data at volume, and update the "last reviewed" date
 * below whenever it changes.
 */
const LAST_REVIEWED = "July 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What personal information we collect, why, how long we keep it, and how to ask us to delete it. Including our photo consent practice for schools."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Privacy policy"
    lead={`What we collect, why we collect it, and how to make us delete it. Last reviewed ${LAST_REVIEWED}.`}
  />

  <section class="section grain">
    <div class="shell-narrow prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        We collect the least we can. We use it only to do the work described on
        this site. We do not sell it, rent it, or share it for advertising. If you
        want it deleted, email{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.general}`}>{SITE.email.general}</a> and we
        will do it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is {SITE.legalStatus.toLowerCase()} based in{" "}
        {SITE.location.line}. We are the data controller for the information
        described here. For any privacy question, contact{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.general}`}>{SITE.email.general}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>

      <h3>School applications</h3>
      <p>
        When a school applies for a library we collect the school's name and
        address, its type and enrolment, a contact person's name, role, email and
        phone number, a description of the library space, the reason for
        applying, and optionally photographs of the space.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use this solely to assess and administer library projects. We store it
        securely and we do not share it with third parties except as needed to
        deliver the programme — for example, sharing a shortlisted school's
        address with the local delivery partner who will carry out the
        refurbishment.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>How long we keep it.</strong> Applications from schools we take
        on are retained for the life of the project and for seven years
        afterwards, because Canadian charity law requires us to keep records
        demonstrating how funds were used. Applications we do not take forward are
        deleted within 24 months, unless you ask us to keep you on file for a
        future cohort.
      </p>

      <h3>Enquiries and partnership messages</h3>
      <p>
        Your name, email address, organisation if you give one, and your message.
        We use it to reply to you and to keep a record of the conversation. Kept
        for three years, then deleted.
      </p>

      <h3>Mailing list</h3>
      <p>
        If you sign up for updates we keep your email address until you
        unsubscribe. Every email we send includes an unsubscribe link, and
        unsubscribing removes your address entirely.
      </p>

      <h3>Donations</h3>
      {
        DONATE.url ? (
          <p>
            Donations are handled by{" "}
            <strong>{DONATE.platformName || "our donation provider"}</strong>, not
            by this website. Payment details are entered there, and AVID never
            sees or stores them. We receive your name, the amount, and the contact
            details you choose to share, which we use to acknowledge your gift and
            send you the report on the school it funded.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            We have not yet connected an online donation platform, so this website
            does not collect or process any payment information at all. Gifts are
            currently arranged by email, and we keep only what we need to
            acknowledge the gift and report on how it was used.
          </p>
        )
      }
      <p>
        Donation records are kept for seven years, as required for Canadian
        financial and charity reporting.
      </p>

      <h2>Photographs of schools and children</h2>
      <p>
        We publish photographs of the libraries we build. This is central to our
        transparency, and it carries a duty we take seriously.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          We obtain <strong>written consent from the school</strong> before
          publishing any photograph taken on its premises.
        </li>
        <li>
          Where an identifiable child appears, we obtain{" "}
          <strong>written consent from that child's parent or guardian</strong>,
          in addition to the school's. Consent is specific about where the image
          may be used.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not publish a child's full name alongside their photograph, and we
          do not publish images that reveal a child's home address, school
          timetable or other identifying detail.
        </li>
        <li>
          Consent can be withdrawn at any time. Email{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.general}`}>{SITE.email.general}</a> and we
          will remove the image from the site, usually within two working days.
        </li>
        <li>
          Where we have not obtained consent, we publish no photograph. Our
          publishing process blocks it rather than relying on anyone to remember.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Our child protection policy governs all activity conducted in or around
        schools, by us and by our delivery partners.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
      {
        ANALYTICS.plausibleDomain ? (
          <p>
            We use Plausible Analytics to count visits and see which pages are
            useful. It is privacy-focused: it sets{" "}
            <strong>no cookies</strong>, collects no personal data, does not
            track you across websites, and stores no information that could
            identify you. There is nothing to consent to and nothing to opt out
            of, which is why you have not been shown a cookie banner.
          </p>
        ) : NEEDS_COOKIE_CONSENT ? (
          <p>
            We use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages are
            useful. It sets cookies, so we ask your permission first — the
            notice you saw when you arrived. Google Analytics does not load at
            all unless you accept. If you declined, or ignored the notice,
            nothing was set. You can change your mind by clearing this site's
            data in your browser and reloading the page.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            This site currently runs <strong>no analytics and sets no
            cookies</strong>. We do not track you, and there is no consent
            banner because there is nothing to consent to.
          </p>
        )
      }
      <p>
        Our web host keeps standard server logs, which include IP addresses, for
        a short period for security and troubleshooting. We do not use them to
        build any profile of you.
      </p>

      <h2>Fonts, embeds and third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The fonts on this site are served from our own domain, so loading a page
        does not tell Google or anyone else that you visited. We do not embed
        social media widgets, advertising trackers, or "like" buttons.
      </p>
      <p>Form submissions are delivered through a form-handling service, which processes your message in order to email it to us.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>tell you what information we hold about you;</li>
        <li>correct anything that is wrong;</li>
        <li>delete it, where we are not legally required to keep it;</li>
        <li>stop emailing you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.general}`}>{SITE.email.general}</a>{" "}
        and we will respond within 30 days. If you are not satisfied with our
        response, you may complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of
        Canada.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy we will update the date at the top. Material
        changes affecting how we use information you have already given us will be
        emailed to you where we hold your address.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
